WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.409
Film Courage: What are some things that you
learned in the last five years that you wished

00:00:03.409 --> 00:00:06.270
you knew in the first five years since you
moved here?

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:09.139
Adam William Ward, Actor/Producer/Director
(WALLY GOT WASTED: Some of it plays into things

00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:13.200
I’ve already said but Number 1 is “Bank
in yourself.”

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.690
If you really believe in yourself you have
to bank in yourself.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:21.300
And what that means is you can’t depend
on an external person to make your dreams

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.300
happen.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.430
If you want to make them happen, you go make
them happen with yourself.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:31.019
Now some actors are very much independent
of a studio or a filmmaker if you’re not

00:00:31.019 --> 00:00:32.800
a filmmaker yourself.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.080
But even an actor in a way you could find
the right director.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.079
You could find money people.

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:41.500
You could then produce and put a whole project
together.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.090
But it’s the bank in yourself.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:50.289
It’s to start learning and figure out what
you need to do and do it.

00:00:50.289 --> 00:00:51.300
Do it yourself.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:55.829
WALLY GOT WASTED we did completely outside
of the studio system and it would have never

00:00:55.829 --> 00:01:00.270
got made if I was…I’d still be scratching
my head handing in the script to people and

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:04.290
even though people loved the script I’d
still be handing it to people and even the

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.930
people that might have wanted to make it they
wouldn’t have made me the director.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.509
“Who are you?”

00:01:08.509 --> 00:01:13.439
So I had to do it to learn and prove myself.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:17.970
That’s another thing that I’ve learned
is that people don’t see potential.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:19.600
You have to show them.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.689
I’m the same person I was five or six years
ago when I was telling people I’m going

00:01:24.689 --> 00:01:25.729
to be a film director.

00:01:25.729 --> 00:01:27.430
They don’t really believe me.

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:28.430
They don’t really know.

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:31.090
There are so many people who say things in
this town.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:35.610
Now they treat me with totally different respect
and they look at me like a filmmaker.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:40.590
It’s very interesting in that way, it’s
like you know what you’re going to do or

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:44.040
what you’re capable of, so go do it and
show people.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.240
Don’t trust that they see it too.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:47.980
They are not going to see it, you have to
show them.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:52.979
Film Courage: What you you say to people who
aren’t as confident with themselves?

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:54.630
Maybe they are not confident with the way
that they look?

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:58.950
I mean you’re a handsome man, you’re tall,
you present yourself well, so it’s easy

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:03.130
for me to see why people (aside from talent)
would want to believe in you.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:05.229
But not everybody has that.

00:02:05.229 --> 00:02:08.190
What would you say to people who don’t feel
like they have it?

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:13.290
Adam: It’s funny because that kind of goes
under motivation.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:16.170
I’m actually motivated by people not believing
in me in a way.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:20.360
I mean I have a lot of support and a lot of
my father and my mother and my family believe

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.620
in me a lot.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:25.410
But I’m actually more motivated by people
who tell me I can’t do something.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:32.170
I don’t know how healthy that is but that’s
what it is and I think ultimately you have

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.940
to start looking at yourself.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:39.050
Then the work doesn’t start with making
films, the work starts inner and you need

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:45.190
to go look and analyze yourself and really
build yourself up maybe with positive reinforcement

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:46.410
every morning?

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:48.250
Maybe meditation, whatever it is?

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:53.780
Build yourself up to believe, the belief that
you can do it because without the belief,

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.280
you’re not going to do it.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:01.970
If you believe what people tell you, I think
anybody who has ever done anything amazing,

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:05.410
they were told they can’t do it and if they
believed it, they never would have done it,

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:13.180
so the fact that it’s never been done before
just makes me excited that I’ll be the first.

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:19.870
Film Courage: So it’s more a challenge when
someone polite or not says “No” to you

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:24.120
because then rather than someone who seems
more “Yes, that sounds great.”

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.820
Maybe to you that’s not enough of a challenge?

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.370
Adam: I don’t look forward to it.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:33.150
It’s not like I’m “Oh please tell me
no!”

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:39.040
But it’s kind of like…I don’t know,
it’s a fire inside of you.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:41.760
You tell me “No” and I’m like “Why
do you want to get in my way?

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:45.180
I’m going to win, no matter what.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.950
I’m going to make this happen.”

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.430
And I have good intentions with it.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.380
I’m not trying to defeat anybody.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:04:06.560
But I have my goals and my dreams and my belief
in it is…your belief in you and what you

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:09.410
can do just can’t waiver, it cannot.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:11.340
And that’s the first place to work on.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:15.290
If you don’t have that believe you need
to work on it and get it before you even take

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:23.030
on the beast of a feature or any dream you
have because I’m sure curing cancer, the

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:27.070
people working on it right now believe they’re
going to cure it no matter what.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:29.820
And you couldn’t tell them…you couldn’t
convince them that they weren’t going to

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:32.060
cure it even though they haven’t done it
yet.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:36.320
But that’s the kind of belief that you need
to have and determination to accomplish your

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:37.600
dreams no matter what they are.

